 02CC           ; //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 02CC           ; //  FUNCTION NAME:    iRatioFromCalibration
 02CC           ; //
 02CC           ; //  DESCRIPTION:      Encodes or decodes a ratio measured during calibration 
 02CC           ; //                                    so that the encoded result can be stored in the
 02CC           ; //                                    BYTE arrays [bCalFreqIndex][bLoad] 
 02CC           ; //                                    The measured ratio is first scaled to the true ratio, and then
 02CC           ; //                                    log-like encoding is used to allow (measured/true) to range from
 02CC           ; //                                            1/2 to 2 for (Vr/Vf measured) / (Vr/Vf true) -> -127 to 127 
 02CC           ; //                                            1/5 to 5 for (Vz/Va measured) / (Vz/Va true) -> -127 to 127
 02CC           ; //                                    hence the result can be encoded in an array of signed char.
 02CC           ; //                                    Using signed innteger for the output and inputs means that the
 02CC           ; //                                    single function can be used in each direction (encode & decode)
 02CC           ; //
 02CC           ; //  ARGUMENTS:                xDir            = STORE | RETRIEVE
 02CC           ; //                                    xType           = MODZ | MODGAMMA
 02CC           ; //                                    iRatio_true     = true ratio for the cal point scaled by wUNITY
 02CC           ; //                                    iRatio          = ratio scaled by wUNITY, or encoded value, to convert 
 02CC           ; //
 02CC           ; //  RETURNS:          signed int      = encoded value (range -127 to 127) when encoding
 02CC           ; //                                    signed int      = Measured ratio (range 0 to 32767 scaled by wUNITY) when decoding
 02CC           ; //
 02CC           ; //    NOTES:                  Whilst |Z|/50 can range to 65537/wUNITY, 32767 is enough for
 02CC           ; //                                    the largest calibration load (560 ohms, true ratio 11200/wUNITY)
 02CC           ; //                                    |Gamma| ranges 0 to 1000/wUNITY or slightly over with measurement error
 02CC           ; //                                    The encoded output has zero indicating measured ratio = true ratio, so
 02CC           ; //                                    the calibration table is initialised to zero by default
 02CC           ; //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
